can you successfully follow up one of  the most beloved comic book movies of  all time is it possible to make a dude  with teeny Wings on his feet and little  green shorts look cool the answer is  that yes you can but not without a few  compromises along the way warning Major  Spoilers for black panther wakanda  forever ahead  costume designer Ruth e Carter who  became the first black woman ever to win  the Oscar in the category for her work  on the first black panther has really  outdone herself this time with her  return in Black Panther wakanda forever  the costumes in wakanda Forever range  from college kids streetwear to  high-tech diving suits to ceremonial  funeral Garb and so much more Queen  raimonda's Mini Royal ensembles or  standouts in various shades of jewel  tones from form-fitting to billowing her  gowns all still share the same design  Motif thanks to similar prints and  coordinating jewelry nakia's bright and  casual clothes from her scenes is a  Haitian teacher suit the character's  personality just as much as her vibrant  greenish War Dog armor and the  incredible quality of Neymar's movie  specific design does much of the work of  transforming the character from a long  time Comics Oddball into a mythical  anti-hero god the outfits are all  visually interesting yet believe a and  how they pull inspiration from real  culture ancient and modern is  commendable she really can make you like  click  s with the costume she puts you in she's  a Storyteller for  usually if the camera is going to linger  on a particular shot in an MCU film it's  because of fight choreography or  expensive CGI in wakanda Forever the  camera frequently lingers on characters  just looking awesome in their clothes  Carter's Creations are that breathtaking  while none of the designs in wakanda  Forever are misses the fleet of vehicles  in the film is probably the weakest  element conceptually on their own all  the modes of transportation range from  fine to pretty cool for instance the  aircraft that arrives to transport to  chala's vibranium coffin almost  resembles the face of a black panther  when it's lit up and viewed from below  which is an interesting visual touch but  when it actually levitates the casket up  in its tractor beam during the funeral  it completely takes viewers out of  what's an otherwise serious somber  moment meanwhile some of the other  planes that are deployed to evacuate  citizens during the flooding of wakanda  look vaguely and curiously like simpler  versions of Nova core Starships from the  Guardians of the Galaxy even the large  wakandan ship that serves as the main  Battleground for the film's final fight  feels kind of boring and unmemorable  wakanda forever's vehicles feel marvely  they're just not the sleekest or most  exciting that the MCU has to offer  wakanda forever confronts heavy and  pressing Global issues head-on the film  can be read as a metaphor for nuclear  proliferation the wakandans possess the  world's most powerful resource and  everyone else is in a race to catch up  in the past real civilizations like Nazi  Germany or the Soviet Union have been  the antagonists in Marvel films this  time it's modern America France and the  rest of the United Nations being  outgunned by a small African country has  exposed the West's hypocrisy new CIA  director Valentina Allegra de Fontaine  openly admits she dreams about the U.S  controlling Earth's vibranium Supply but  a large chunk of the international  intelligence Community is willing to  resort to some pretty villainous tactics  to get that sweet magic medal at a  United Nations meeting Queen ramonda  dramatically announces that wakanda has  foiled a plot to steal vibranium from  one of their secret research facilities  by having the Dora milaje March the  captive offenders before their heads of  state she argues it's not vibranium's  power she fears but what humans would do  with it it's a bold move to call out  these nations this way but it works with  the story wakanda forever is trying to  tell the sequel is also interested in  colonialism and its effects on  indigenous people in a flashback we see  that Spanish conquistadors brought ruin  to Neymar's people his anger at and  distrust of the surface World stems from  The Fallout even the film's resolution  in which two super-powered beings agree  to put Vengeance aside and de-escalate  their fight plays into the nuclear  symbolism in The Real World Cold War  policy of mutually assured destruction  wakanda forever's politics aren't left  or right they're clear-eyed and  practical  Dominique Thorne is a likable addition  to the MCU as Riri Williams AKA  ironheart but the plot that introduces  her isn't as good as the character  herself or Thorne's performance it's  entertaining and gives wakanda forever  some propulsion early on but it's also  underbaked that can't be good riri's  vibranium detecting school project ends  up in the hands of covert U.S operatives  who are using it to find heretofore  unknown quantities of vibranium from a  seabed in the Atlantic Ocean this  interference threatens Neymar and his  people's way of life and kicks off the  conflict between Neymar and wakanda  Neymar wants to kill the scientists who  made the machine while shuri is  determined to protect Riri unfortunately  riri's actual involvement in the story  doesn't amount to much there's a fun  moment early on where she helps Sharia  nokoye escape the local police with the  help of her homemade ironheart suit but  after that she's little more than a plot  football part hardly anything she does  from this point forward affects the  events of the film her more polished  Iron Heart armor helps shuri's plan to  trap Neymar in the final battle but her  character's motivations aren't much more  than don't die helpful wakanda the movie  keeps trying to tell us that she'll be  important with a few hints of her  backstory but we rarely see that  importance take shape like America  Chavez and Dr Strange in the Multiverse  of Madness Riri is an exciting new  character with tons of potential who's  reduced mostly to a human MacGuffin  one of the smartest decisions Ryan  coogler and company made was swapping  Marvel Comics Atlantis for the mythical  Mesoamerican city of telokon a  fictionalization of talocon one of the  Aztec afterlives of course the decision  was more or less made for them since  Warner Brothers beat Marvel to the  screen with Aquaman never mind that  Neymar came first in the comics Aquaman  has always been the better known  Half-Blood king of Atlantis wakanda  forever changed that bit of Neymar's  backstory and it works wonderfully in  the film version his origin story has  everything to do with a vibranium  meteorite and Spanish conquistadors  rooting Namor in Aztec and Mayan history  and culture is a vast Improvement on an  already intriguing Comics character and  the telecon that the filmmakers created  for him Rivals wakanda born with  prolonged life and the ability to  breathe air and water as well as the  gift of flight because of the Wings on  his feet Namor is given the title kukul  Khan or feather serpent God a  supernatural entity pulled from  Mesoamerican religion as a boy he  becomes a legend to his people when he  uses his power to fight back against  Spanish colonizers since the MCU has  been interested in geopolitical issues  and gods lately this updated version of  Neymar and his home of telecon fits  right into the Cinematic universe's  trajectory  koye became one of the breakout  characters in Black Panther for good  reason the leader of the doer milaje was  as stoic and tough as anyone in the  first film say for t'challa himself her  storyline saw her wrestle with the  question of what to do when killmonger  assumed the throne though dinagarira is  every bit as captivating in wakanda  Forever the film doesn't do her justice  she gets a stunning entrance when the  Dora milaje infiltrate the French  operatives planning to steal and study  vibranium but for much of the second  half of the movie She's M.I.A when shuri  and Riri are captured ramonda blames  Okoye and dismisses her from Duty  devastated one of the best characters  and best actors in the film is sidelined  in a movie with way too many characters  to fully develop it's a shame that one  of the franchise's best doesn't get  enough screen time to continue her own  fascinating story  in the comics Neymar and black panther  have a real love-hate relationship  sometimes they align themselves and  their kingdoms with each other for a  common cause and they are both  superhuman rulers of super secret  societies but more often than not  they're at each other's throats with  wakanda forever somebody other than  t'challa had to put on The Black  Panther's mask and face off against  Neymar though Chadwick Boseman and tanak  Huerta would have been phenomenal scene  partners aweta and Leticia writes shuri  have a totally different chemistry that  takes Neymar and the Black Panthers love  hate relationship to another level in  this adaptation there's actually some  romantic tension between the mutant god  king and the scientist princess it's  never made explicit except for that  pretty high value gift of his Beloved  Mother's bracelet when Namor offers to  take Sharita talukan and wistfully  confides in her that she's the first  surface human ever to have seen their  world it's not hard to imagine them as  Allah and maybe something more there's a  tragic irony to the idea that these two  understand each other but are destined  to become enemies for a time at least  when rimanda orders Nakia to invade his  home and she kills some of his people to  rescue shuri he retaliates by flooding  wakanda and indirectly killing many  citizens including ramonda herself even  their final showdown is charged with  shared emotion they're both isolated  angry and as Neymar's name means in this  take on the character without love but  if only broken people can be great  leaders there are big things ahead for  Neymar and shuri together or not both  nations want the same thing which is to  preserve and to protect their people but  they're willing to go by different ways  when the MCU first took us to wakanda  viewers got to meet a plethora of new  characters including more people of  color and more women than the franchise  had ever seen before in addition to  t'challa his Supporting Cast all had  unique fleshed out personalities of  their own wakanda forever advertised  that audiences would become acquainted  with a second super-powered civilization  the trailers and casting news indicated  that atuma and nomura two important  characters from the comics would be  living and fighting alongside Namor just  as a koye and umbaku did in Black  Panther in the comics atuma is a  barbarian-like Atlantean who believes  that he ought to rule instead of Namor  and throughout her comics history nomura  has been everything from neymore's  implied lover to his cousin to a clone  even with the change from Atlantis to  telecon there is enough backstory to  have made a Tuma and the Mora more  unique characters instead one of wakanda  forever's weak spots is the regrettable  underdevelopment of his telecono  Supporting Cast there deployed much like  Infinity Wars ebony Ma and Proxima  midnight like a henchman and henchwoman  who are little more than bodies in the  way until it's time for the main  characters to fight Neymar we get little  more than a hint that nomura is  dissatisfied with Namor and shury's  peaceful resolution near the end  it's become a refrain that most Marvel  movies are great until the Final Act  evolves into a CGI soup the main  ingredients of which are faceless hordes  Kaiju like Monsters and of course Sky  beams and portals most of the criticism  of the first black panther in fact came  for its lackluster last act digital  effects it seems the filmmakers have  learned from their mistakes and from  worn out MCU tropes the final battle in  wakanda Forever is one of Marvel Studios  shorter and smaller scale scuffles but  in terms of relevance to the plot and  visual style it's a breath of fresh air  Sherry finally steps into a leadership  role as the Black Panther literally  standing as the Vanguard of her troops  atop a massive military vessel they're  planning to lure Namor to them so they  can trap him into a retrofitted aircraft  that will dry him out and deplete his  powers just as Namor is his people's god  of the air Land and Sea this climactic  conflict unfolds in the sky sand and on  the Atlantic Riri Williams gleefully  buzzes through the clouds in her tricked  out ironheart suit shuri crashed lands  on the shore and the Black Panther and  The Feathered Serpent God slash at each  other acrobatically in the sand and  Flames the Dora milage used cables to  take on the teleconil in an impressively  choreographed vertical assault while the  Jabari defend the deck it's perfect for  the story that wakanda forever is trying  to tell which is about how war is rarely  in a nation's best interest  this might sound like a backhanded  compliment but the mcu's Namor looks way  cooler than anyone who's familiar with  Comics probably expected in his earliest  Illustrated form Namor looks like a turn  of the century muscle man in a belted  Speedo and then there's the matter of  those pointy elf ears and those little  angelic wings that grow out of his feet  even after Namor got an emo makeover in  the 2000s writers and artists still had  to contend with those quirks as did Ryan  coogler in wakanda forever as per usual  the writer director was up to the task  Namor is one of the highlights of the  movie my enemies call me no more  in part that's thanks to the casting of  tenoch Huerta and his performance which  ranges from endearing to frightening and  in part that's thanks to the character's  new backstory and status as an  indigenous Mexican god king Neymar still  has his skimpy green shorts but the  costume has been redesigned with Native  iconography and materials somehow even  the image of the mutant hovering in  place is Tiny foot Wings flapping fast  isn't ridiculous all of this is an  enormous accomplishment considering how  often Namor looks silly in the comic  books and how serious wakanda forever is  for most of its run time the only  moments in which it's hard to take the  movie and its anti-hero seriously come  when the mutant Leaps and Bounds through  set pieces like Legolas doing parkour or  when he uses his winged feet to dash  across the sky not unlike a hummingbird  CGI has come a long way but it still  can't make superhuman Feats like that  look very natural  [Music]
 

